   "text": "This is sertraline hydrochloride, a 1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene core with these features:\n\n- **C1:** carries an NHCH3 group on a wedge bond.\n- **C4:** carries a 3,4-dichlorophenyl group, also on a wedge bond, so the two substituents are cis.\n- **Salt:** the HCl is written as a separate component.\n\nI assigned the stereocentres from the drawing, with the implicit hydrogen pointing back at each:\n\n- **C1:** the priorities are N > aromatic ring carbon C8a > CH2. N \u2192 C8a \u2192 C2 runs counterclockwise, so C1 is S.\n- **C4:** the priorities are C4a > aryl ipso carbon > CH2. C4a is ranked above the aryl carbon because its highest branch, C8a, has substituents (C,C,C) against (C,C,H) for the aryl ortho carbons. C4a \u2192 aryl \u2192 C3 runs counterclockwise, so C4 is S.\n\nThis gives the (1S,4S) configuration. I wrote the SMILES for that configuration from memory of sertraline's known SMILES and did not re-derive the @/@@ symbols atom by atom.\n\nSMILES: CN[C@H]1CC[C@@H](c2ccc(Cl)c(Cl)c2)c2ccccc12.Cl"
